# Build output.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so these match ONLY at the repository root. An
# unanchored `build/` matches a directory of that name at any depth, which had
# been silently excluding all of scripts/build/ -- the Linux verification matrix
# and the Graphify refresh scripts were never committed, even though CLAUDE.md
# documents them as the way to run those steps. A fresh clone had neither.
/build/
/out/
/cmake-build-*/
_deps/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Compiled objects
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.so
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Generated / large data — NOT versioned (see README "Git discipline")
datasets/raw/
datasets/processed/
models/checkpoints/
models/exported/

# Training sets are derived: lpq_collect regenerates them exactly from the
# graph and the query manifest, both of which ARE versioned. The NY set alone
# is ~30 MB, and a file that can be rebuilt byte-for-byte from committed inputs
# is not worth carrying in history.
models/training/
experiments/runs/

# Raw benchmark output is immutable but not committed by default.
# Paper-frozen results are force-added deliberately.
results/raw/
results/processed/
results/figures/
results/tables/

# LPQ Atlas runtime artifacts: run/benchmark job directories and the
# exported-array cache, all regenerable.
results/atlas/
# libFuzzer working corpora (CI)
/corpus/

# Graphify knowledge-graph output (regenerable from source)
graphify-out/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
